+class LatticeDraftSampler:
+    """The top-16 lattice proposal, folded into the draft cuda graph.
+
+    WHY THIS EXISTS.  DsparkDraftSampler above folds the FULL-VOCABULARY sequential walk,
+    and refuses arms that propose over a candidate lattice or whose head reads the
+    committed prefix.  Both refusals were about that kernel, not about folding: a lattice
+    arm was left on the eager path, and measured at bs=1 it paid ~5.5 ms of draft per
+    round against ~1.9 ms for the folded vanilla checkpoint on the same box -- while
+    reading a HIGHER accept length.  At bs=1 the round is dispatch-bound, so an unfolded
+    proposal is not a serving configuration at all.
+
+    WHY THE LATTICE IS FOLDABLE AT ALL.  build_markov_lattice's own docstring makes the
+    argument: the predecessor enters through the previous token alone, and for the
+    attention head the keys are the committed prefix, which no predecessor changes.  So
+    every (slot, predecessor) edge is independent -- one batched call, then a walk over a
+    precomputed table.  The sequential dependence is between TABLE LOOKUPS, not between
+    GPU launches.  DFLASH already folds exactly this shape (_SelectorDraftSampler), and
+    build_markov_lattice shares its predecessor indexing and edge einsum.
+
